        "original_id": "4939c8c9-fef0-5e46-8ee2-18830d57fcb6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stephen Pearcy, Alexander O'Neal, Al Pitrelli, Hiro Kuretani, Jimmy Jam, Terry Lewis\n- Bands/Projects: Ratt, Vertex, Arcade, Vicious Delite, Nitronic, Danger Danger, Hotshot, Alice Cooper, Asia, Savatage, Megadeth, Trans-Siberian Orchestra, WXXI, Trancentral Station\n- Songs: \"What's Missing\"\n- Places: Natchez, Mississippi\n\nFacts:\n- Alexander O'Neal was born on November 15, 1953, and he is an American R&B singer, songwriter, and arranger from Natchez, Mississippi.\n- Stephen Eric Pearcy was born on July 3, 1956, and he is an American musician known as Stephen Pearcy.\n- Stephen Pearcy is best known as the founder, singer, and songwriter of the heavy metal band Ratt.\n- Vertex was a band formed in 1995 featuring singer Stephen Pearcy, guitarist Al Pitrelli, and drummer Hiro Kuretani.\n- Stephen Pearcy was associated with Ratt, Arcade, Vicious Delite, and Nitronic.\n- Al Pitrelli was associated with Danger Danger, Hotshot, Alice Cooper, Asia, Savatage, Megadeth, and Trans-Siberian Orchestra.\n- Hiro Kuretani was associated with WXXI and Trancentral Station.\n- \"What's Missing\" is a song written by Jimmy Jam and Terry Lewis and recorded by American recording artist Alexander O'Neal.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
